# Task: Backup script

Write an executable bash script at `{{script_path}}` that creates a compressed backup of a directory.

The script takes exactly two arguments:

1. the path of the source directory
2. the path of an existing destination directory

The script must create a gzip-compressed tar archive inside the destination directory, named `{{archive_prefix}}-<NAME>.tar.gz`, where `<NAME>` is the base name of the source directory (for example, for the source `/opt/data`, the archive is named `{{archive_prefix}}-data.tar.gz`). The archive must contain all files of the source directory with their contents intact, and the script must exit with status code `0` on success.

A sample data directory is available at `{{source_dir}}` for testing.
